  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 651(a), a simple trust must distribute all income currently. The trust must distribute the full $50,000 to claim the income distribution deduction under Sec. 651(b), which eliminates the income from the trust''s taxable base.
Wrong (A): Distributing $0 would leave all income taxable to the trust. A simple trust has no discretion to retain current income.
