  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 661(a), a complex trust''s income distribution deduction equals the lesser of DNI or amounts actually distributed. Here DNI is $60,000 and the distribution is $30,000, so the deduction is $30,000. The remaining DNI is retained and taxed at trust rates.
Wrong (B): $60,000 is the full DNI, but the deduction is limited to the amount actually distributed ($30,000), not the full DNI.
Wrong (C): $80,000 is the trust''s taxable income before the deduction. The distribution deduction cannot exceed DNI or actual distributions.
