-- Q4250: Trusts and Estates [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 676, a trust is treated as a grantor trust when the grantor retains the power to revoke the trust and recover trust assets. This power means the grantor can reclaim the property, so all income is taxed directly to the grantor under Sections 671-679.
Wrong (A): The power to distribute income to charities does not trigger grantor trust status. This is a fiduciary distribution power, not a retained beneficial interest.
Wrong (B): Appointing a successor trustee is an administrative power that does not give the grantor beneficial ownership or control over trust income.
Wrong (C): Allocating receipts between income and principal is a standard trustee accounting function that does not trigger grantor trust treatment.$EXPL$
