-- Q4251: Trusts and Estates [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 677, if trust income may be distributed or held for the grantor''s benefit (including paying premiums on the grantor''s life insurance), the income is taxable to the grantor. Grantor trust rules override normal trust taxation.
Wrong (A): The trust is not the taxable entity when grantor trust rules apply. Section 677 attributes income directly to the grantor.
Wrong (B): The beneficiaries are not taxed on grantor trust income. The grantor trust rules under Sections 671-679 take priority over the normal distribution rules.
